    "content": "\"Arctic Frost\" refers primarily to a controversial FBI investigation, though it is also used in commercial contexts. As of March 2026, the investigation is the subject of active, high-level Senate oversight. 1. \"Arctic Frost\" Investigation (Politics/News) Definition: \"Arctic Frost\" was the codename for a FBI/DOJ investigation initiated in April 2022 (during the Biden administration) that targeted efforts to overturn the 2020 election. Scope: According to Senate Judiciary Committee records, the investigation became a wide-ranging probe that targeted over 400 Republican organizations and individuals, including nine members of Congress. Controversy & Findings: Senator Chuck Grassley has characterized the operation as a \"fishing expedition\" and a \"modern Watergate,\" alleging it was used to improperly monitor political opponents. Documents suggest phone records were subpoenaed for numerous GOP lawmakers, including Sens. Lindsey Graham, Josh Hawley, and others. Accountability & Recent Developments (2025-2026): Following reports by Sen. Grassley, FBI Director Kash Patel (appointed after the 2024 election) fired employees involved in the investigation and dismantled the \"CR-15\" squad responsible for it. As of March 2026, fired agents are suing over their termination, and the Senate is conducting hearings on the investigation's abuse of power. 2. Other \"Arctic Frost\" References Agriculture: The 'Arctic Frost' Satsuma is a cold-hardy citrus hybrid, often grown in Texas, known for being a sweet and tart, easy-to-peel fruit. Product: \"Gatorade Frost Arctic Blitz\" is a popular, berry-flavored sports drink. Product: \"Arctic Frost\" is a type of light blue pearl automotive paint basecoat. Product: \"Arctic Frost\" is a type of wall art featuring polar bears. Note: This information is accurate as of March 25, 2026, based on the provided search results.",
